                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This was way better than I expected looking and the previews on the store page.\nThis is a full fledged adventure clearly inspired from The Adventures of Link.\n\nThe items and spells that are fun to use which will allow you to progress in the game's world or fight enemies more easily.\n\nThere's a lot of backtracking to do when you find new items so you will have to revisit locations you already went through multiple times to get everything. It's fun to explore and discover new location and items but there's a lot of running in circle and time wasted that could have been avoided with a better map. The maps are also not very clearly defined which makes it hard to come back in zones to \n\nThere is no name of the region you're in when you look on the map so even when you try to look up guides and stuff online, it will be quite hard to know where you are, which is kinda annoying and a bit frustrating.\n\nThey didn't bother updating the game with the conveniences offered on the other platforms, mainly more inventory slots to use utility items like potions and the feather, the later being used to fast travel doesn't have the map included in other versions that allows you to select where you want to go around the world, which is kinda lame to be honest but doesn't detract from how good the game is.\n\nThe music is really good with vibes similar to old-school J-RPGs in the overworld, Zelda dungeons in the dungeons and one that sounds a lot like Gerudo Valley too. Gotta love that.\n\nDespite some flaws, I really recommend it to anyone who wants to have an experience similar to the Old-School Zelda 2 but on the easier side.",
